note The xtask binary: the owner's rulebook as a program. cargo xtask is an alias in .cargo/config.toml that runs this crate with its own target directory, so the gate never waits on the workspace's build lock and a broken workspace build cannot break the tool that reports it. Five tasks: gate (the gate path), lint (archlint over the workspace or named files), api (record the API lock), words (identifier words missing from vocabulary.txt) and hook (the Claude Code hooks). The whole directory is rulebook: an agent may run every task but change none of them, which is what makes the rules binding on the agent that is being checked. A task answers with a Message on success or failure; main prints the first to stdout and the second to stderr and exits non-zero on failure, so a hook or a shell sees the verdict in the exit code.

